# Jaguar Mark V 2 1/2 and 3 1/2 Litre four-door saloon, 1948-1951.
#
# The first post-war Jaguar saloon: separate front wings with the headlamps in
# teardrop housings on top, a tall narrow radiator grille with close-set vertical
# bars, a two-piece flat windscreen, six-light body, rear wheel spats and a chrome
# waist moulding. The 2 1/2 and 3 1/2 Litre saloons are externally identical apart
# from badges and tyres, so one shell represents both.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_V
#
# Dimensions 4.762 x 1.765 x 1.588 m, wheelbase 3.048 m (The Motor road test, 1949).
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a silver saloon, but the front
# bumper and leading edge of the wing are clipped by the frame edge; the extreme
# nose is taken from the front three-quarter and the frontal detail. Recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c), the 1948 Foleshill colour-scheme list quoted second-hand.
# Black, Birch Grey, Silver and Cream are period Jaguar names. Weights 2, 2, 1, 1,
# total 6: a low-volume luxury saloon, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 145 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 3,4.
# Dates 1948-1951 production, road tail staggered 1966-1968.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk5.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk5.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-mk5/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 2.0/4.0 and CC BY 2.0).
#
# Accepted deviations: the side photograph clips the front bumper and the
# leading edge of the front wing, so the extreme nose follows the front
# three-quarter and the frontal detail. Radiator bar count and lamp bezel detail
# are simplified at sprite scale. No shape-defining feature was omitted.


